---
import ComparisonTable from "~/components/illustration-kit/ComparisonTable.astro"
import IllustrationFigure from "~/components/illustration-kit/IllustrationFigure.astro"
import Panel from "~/components/illustration-kit/Panel.astro"
---

<IllustrationFigure lead="Two prisoners. Two choices each. Fewer years in prison is better.">
  <ComparisonTable
    caption="Years in prison (A first, B second)"
    columns={["A's choice", "B stays silent", "B testifies"]}
    rows={[
      ["A stays silent", "1, 1", "3, 0"],
      ["A testifies", "0, 3", "2, 2"],
    ]}
    align="center"
    dense
  />

  <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
    <p class="font-bold">1. Think about your own sentence</p>
    <p class="text-base">Whatever B does, A gets fewer years by testifying.</p>
    <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <Panel accent="blue" title="If B stays silent">
        <p class="mt-2 text-base">
          A gets 1 year by staying silent, but <strong>0 years by testifying.</strong>
        </p>
      </Panel>
      <Panel accent="blue" title="If B testifies">
        <p class="mt-2 text-base">
          A gets 3 years by staying silent, but <strong>2 years by testifying.</strong>
        </p>
      </Panel>
    </div>
    <p class="text-base">
      The same is true for B. This reasoning tells both prisoners to testify.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
    <p class="font-bold">2. Think about two prisoners who reason alike</p>
    <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <Panel accent="red" title="Both testify">
        <p class="mt-2 text-xl font-bold">2 years each</p>
      </Panel>
      <Panel accent="green" title="Both stay silent">
        <p class="mt-2 text-xl font-bold">1 year each</p>
      </Panel>
    </div>
    <p class="text-base">
      If they reason alike and make the same choice, staying silent gives both a shorter
      sentence. So why would both choose to testify?
    </p>
  </div>

  <Fragment slot="caption">
    Everyone agrees on the sentences. The disagreement is about what rational players should do:
    choose the better result against either fixed choice, or take seriously that another person
    who reasons just like you may choose as you do.
  </Fragment>
</IllustrationFigure>
